    coordinates: { lat: 34.0480, lng: 74.3805 },
    answer:
        "Gulmarg, the 'Meadow of Flowers', is a high-altitude resort town at about 2,650 metres in the Pir Panjal range of Jammu & Kashmir, roughly 50 km from Srinagar. It is India's premier ski destination and home to the Gulmarg Gondola, one of the world's highest cable cars, which climbs in two stages to Kongdoori and the shoulder of Apharwat Peak near 3,980 metres. Its summer meadows hold one of the world's highest golf courses and the colonial St. Mary's Church. MyTripMyTravel runs Gulmarg as a chauffeured alpine mission — the gondola, the meadows or the ski slopes by season, and a warm valley base.",
    intro: [
        "Gulmarg is a broad alpine bowl in the Pir Panjal, ringed by fir forest and snow peaks and named for the wildflowers that carpet it in summer — the 'Meadow of Flowers'. Sultan Yusuf Shah Chak is said to have renamed the earlier Gaurimarg for its blooms, and the British later turned the meadow into a hill retreat, leaving behind the small stone St. Mary's Church and one of the world's highest golf courses.",
        "Today Gulmarg is best known for the Gulmarg Gondola, a two-stage cable car that lifts visitors first to Kongdoori and then to the flank of Apharwat Peak near 3,980 metres — in winter, the launch point for some of Asia's finest lift-served and off-piste skiing. In summer the same slopes soften into meadow walks, pony trails to Khilanmarg, and the frozen-then-thawing Alpather Lake beneath Apharwat.",
        "MyTripMyTravel runs Gulmarg by season. In winter we stage the ski days with certified guides and attention to avalanche conditions; in the greener months we build meadow drives, gentle treks, and gondola rides for the high views. The high altitude and mountain weather are respected throughout — the gondola can close on short notice, and our planners keep the day flexible.",
    ],
